; expect 72
; Integer division by zero. `sdiv`/`srem` with a zero divisor is
; UNDEFINED in LLVM, and the two targets disagreed about what undefined
; looks like: on darwin-aarch64 this program printed `1` and exited 0,
; and the same IR on linux-x86_64 lowers to `idiv`, which raises
; SIGFPE. Same source, two behaviours, and `check` had nothing to say
; about either - so a program developed on macOS and shipped to Linux
; changed its meaning on the way.
;
; It now names the fault on fd 2 and exits 72, on every target. The
; divisor comes from a function so that no constant folding can decide
; it before the guard does.
(:: zero Int)

(fn (zero) 0)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (/ 10 zero))
